<title>MEXICO: Femsa president said recovering.</title>
<headline>Femsa president said recovering.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican holding company Fondo Economico Mexicano SA (Femsa) president Eugenio Garza Laguera is still in hospital recovering from a recent heart attack, but his health is improving, the company said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;He is getting better; he is very well, but still under observation and resting.... We don't know when he will be back here, but he is keeping in touch with everything through his son-in-law,&quot; Garza's secretary, Lorena Coindreau, said in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>Garza, aged 73 years, suffered a heart attack on April 11. Garza is also president of Grupo Financiero Bancomer and his son-in-law, Jose Antonio Fernandez, is director general of Femsa.</p>
<p>((--Jacqueline Lerma, Monterrey bureau +528 345-7677))</p>
